\subsection{Spectral Trajectory Characterization}
\label{sec:spectral_trajectory}

The Phase~0 pure-synthetic pilot (seed 42, $r_t = 0\;\forall\, t$) reveals a three-stage spectral trajectory across Generations~0--5: anisotropy decompression, decompression peak, and sustained collapse.  Figure~\ref{fig:spectral_trajectory} visualizes this progression.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/spectral_trajectory.pdf}
\caption{Spectral trajectory across recursive generations (Pythia-410M, Generations~0--5). (a) Effective rank peaks at Gen~2 then declines monotonically. (b) Log-determinant shows larger relative decline, confirming tail-spectrum sensitivity. (c) Perplexity accelerates upward. (d) Lexical diversity (Distinct-4) contracts monotonically. Dashed line: Gen~1 baseline.}
\label{fig:spectral_trajectory}
\end{figure}

